 "pair": "ru-en",
 "title": "Живой гусь  (The Live Goose)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "nastya": "Настя",
  "sasha": "Саша"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "In the back hallway, Nastya has found something in a delivery box: a live goose. When she hears the chef intends to cook it, she decides to save it, and Sasha helps her work out how. Here's the Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Саша, иди скорее сюда!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Что случилось, Настя?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Посмотри, в коробке сидит живой гусь!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Откуда здесь взялся этот гусь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Шеф хотел приготовить из него блюдо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Ты решила спасти эту птицу?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Да, я не могу его бросить.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Шеф будет в ярости, если узнает!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Я спрячу гуся в безопасное место.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Только делай это очень осторожно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Его чуть не нашли гости.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Унеси его с кухни прямо сейчас!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Я найду для него тёплый угол.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "И возвращайся скорее к работе!",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now Nastya's rescue.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Саша, иди скорее сюда!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Sasha, come here quickly!' Observe how ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "иди",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "сюда!",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally translates to 'go to here', the normal way to call someone over. The word for 'faster' is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "скорее",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", to hurry them along.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Что случилось, Настя?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What happened, Nastya?' Observe how ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Что",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "случилось,",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'what happened?', the question for anything gone wrong. It is built from the word for an event.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Посмотри, в коробке сидит живой гусь!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Look, a live goose is sitting in the box!' The word for 'have a look' is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Посмотри,",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ". Russians say a goose ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "сидит",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", sits, in a box, and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "в",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "коробке",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'in the box'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Откуда здесь взялся этот гусь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Where did this goose come from?' Asking where from takes its own word: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Откуда",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", next to the word for where, and where to. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "взялся",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is an action word built from taking, and the ending turns 'took' into 'turned up out of nowhere'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Шеф хотел приготовить из него блюдо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The chef wanted to prepare a dish out of it.' Looking closely, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "из",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "него",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'out of him', since the word for a goose is a male animal shape, with an extra letter added. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "хотел",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "приготовить",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'wanted to prepare'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Ты решила спасти эту птицу?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Did you decide to save this bird?' We can hear ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "решила",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to decided, with an ending for a woman. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "спасти",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", the word for to save, shares a root with the word for thank you, and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "птицу?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'bird'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Да, я не могу его бросить.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yes, I cannot abandon him.' Here we see ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "бросить.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to both 'throw' and 'abandon'. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "его",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'him', the goose.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Шеф будет в ярости, если узнает!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The chef will be furious if he finds out!' You will hear ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "будет",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "в",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "ярости,",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally translates to 'will be in fury'. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "узнает!",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", finds out, is built from the word for to know, with a little extra at the start.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Я спрячу гуся в безопасное место.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I will hide the goose in a safe place.' In Russian, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "безопасное",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", safe, is built from the word for without, plus the word for dangerous. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "спрячу",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'I will hide'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Только делай это очень осторожно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Just do it very carefully.' Observe how ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Только",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "делай",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "это",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'only do it'. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "осторожно.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", carefully, is the how-word built from the word for careful.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Его чуть не нашли гости.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The guests almost found him.' We can hear ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "чуть",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "не",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally translates to 'barely not', meaning 'almost'. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "нашли",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'found', and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "гости.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", the word for the guests, comes last.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Унеси его с кухни прямо сейчас!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Carry him away from the kitchen right now!' Listen carefully, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Унеси",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", carry away, is built from the word for to carry, with a piece that means 'away'. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "с",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "кухни",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'off the kitchen', with a matching shape for the last letter.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Я найду для него тёплый угол.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I will find a warm corner for him.' In Russian, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "для",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "него",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'for him', with the extra letter again. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "тёплый",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "угол.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'warm corner', and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "найду",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'I will find'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "И возвращайся скорее к работе!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And return to work quickly!' Focusing here, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "возвращайся",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", the word for come back, has a special ending. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "к",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "работе!",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'towards work', with a matching shape at the end. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Саша, иди скорее сюда!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Что случилось, Настя?",
   "gap": 0.5
